</form><html xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xmlns:math="java.lang.Math" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xs="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" xmlns:fo="http://www.w3.org/1999/XSL/Format" xmlns:fn="http://www.w3.org/2005/02/xpath-functions" xmlns:xdt="http://www.w3.org/2005/02/xpath-datatypes" xmlns:caml="http://lc.ca.gov/legalservices/schemas/caml.1#" xmlns:xhtml="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><title>SB1188:v98#DOCUMENT</title><meta name="dc:identifier" content="SB1188"/><meta name="dc:title" content="SB &#xA;              1188-&#xA;                AMENDED&#xA;              "/><meta http-equiv="Content-Type" content="text/html;charset=utf-8"/></head><body><span class="hidden"><h2>Bill Start</h2></span><div id="bill_all" align="justify"><div id="about"><br clear="all"/><div align="center"><table style="border-collapse: collapse" cellSpacing="0" align="center" role="presentation"><tbody><tr><td align="center"><span style=" text-transform: uppercase; font-size: 1em">
                Amended
               IN </span><span style=" text-transform: uppercase; font-size: 1em">
                Senate
              </span> <span style="text-transform: uppercase">April 09, 2026</span><br/></td></tr></tbody><tbody><tr><td align="center"/></tr></tbody></table></div><br clear="all"/><div align="center"><font size="3" style="FONT-FAMILY: MinionPC, Arial Unicode MS">
                    CALIFORNIA LEGISLATURE—
                    2025–2026 REGULAR SESSION</font></div><br clear="all"/><span id="bill_house_num"><div style="float: left; width:50%; font-weight: bold; "><span style="text-transform: uppercase; text-align:left;width:50%;"><b>
                Senate Bill
              </b></span></div><div style="float:right; width:50%; text-align:right;"><span style="text-transform: uppercase;"><b>No. 1188</b></span></div></span><hr/><br clear="all"/><div align="center"><table style="border-collapse: collapse" cellSpacing="0" align="center" role="presentation"><tbody><tr><td id="bill_authors" align="center"><span style="font-weight:bold;">Introduced by Senator Archuleta<br/></span></td></tr><tr><td id="bill_intro_date" align="center" class="textcenter"><br/>February 19, 2026</td></tr></tbody></table></div><hr/><br clear="all"/><div id="title"><span style="font-weight:normal;font-size:0.9em;"> An act to amend Section 51750 of the Education Code, relating to pupil instruction. </span></div><br clear="all"/><br clear="all"/><div align="center"><h2>LEGISLATIVE COUNSEL'S DIGEST</h2></div><br/><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0"><span id="subject">SB 1188, as amended, Archuleta.
                          Junior Reserve Officers’ Training Corps: home instruction, independent study, and private schools.</span></div><div><span id="digesttext"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">Existing law authorizes the governing board of a school district maintaining a secondary school to establish in the school courses in military science and tactics that comply with provisions of federal law regarding Reserve Officers Training Corps units in educational institutions.</div><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">This bill would revise and recast those provisions by authorizing the governing board or body of a school district, county office of education, or charter school to establish in its schoolsites courses in military science and tactics that comply with provisions of federal law regarding Junior Reserve Officers’ Training Corps (JROTC) units in educational institutions.</div><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">Existing federal law requires a public secondary educational institution that maintains a JROTC unit to permit membership in the unit to homeschooled students
			 residing in the area served by the institution who are qualified for membership in the unit but for lack of enrollment in the institution.</div><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">This bill would require a local educational agency offering a JROTC program within any of its schools to<font color="#B30000"><strike> ensure equal access to</strike></font><font color="blue" class="blue_text"><i> permit membership in</i></font> the JROTC<font color="#B30000"><strike> program, as defined, to</strike></font><font color="blue" class="blue_text"><i> program for homeschooled</i></font> pupils who reside within the attendance area of the local educational<font color="#B30000"><strike> agency and are homeschooled or enrolled in a private school, independent study, or a public school other than the school offering the JROTC program,</strike></font><font color="blue" class="blue_text"><i>
			 agency,</i></font> if those pupils meet all applicable eligibility requirements for participation in the JROTC program other than enrollment in the school offering the JROTC program.</div><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">The bill would require the State Department of Education to make information about existing JROTC programs available on its internet website and distribute implementation guidance to local educational agencies on an annual basis.</div></span></div><span class="hidden"><h2>Digest Key</h2></span><span id="vote">
      Vote:
      <span style=" text-transform: lowercase">MAJORITY</span>  </span><span id="appropriation">
      Appropriation:
      <span style=" text-transform: lowercase">NO</span>  </span><span id="fiscalcommittee">
      Fiscal Committee:
      <span style=" text-transform: lowercase">YES</span>  </span><span id="localprogram">
      Local Program:
      <span style=" text-transform: lowercase">NO</span>  </span></div><hr/><span class="hidden"><h2>Bill Text</h2></span><div id="bill"><div style=" text-transform: uppercase"><h2 style=" text-align: left;">The people of the State of California do enact as follows:</h2><br/></div><div id="s10.006405135071256174"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0" class="ActionLine"><h3 style="font-weight:bold; display:inline;">SECTION 1.</h3> Section 51750 of the Education Code is amended to read:</div><div><div id="id_05975346-62D0-46EF-AD5E-60FA41EBD108"><div><p><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;"><h6 style="display:inline;">51750.</h6> (a) The governing board or body of a local educational agency maintaining a secondary school may establish in its schoolsites courses in military science and tactics complying with the laws of the United States made and provided with reference to Junior Reserve Officers’ Training Corps (JROTC) units in educational institutions.</div><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">(b) A pupil enrolled in a school that establishes courses in military science and tactics pursuant to subdivision (a) shall not be required to enroll in any course in military science and tactics.</div><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">(c) (1) A local educational agency offering a JROTC program within any of its schools
						shall, consistent with Section 2031(f)(1) of Title 10 of the United States Code,<font color="#B30000"><strike> ensure equal access to</strike></font><font color="blue" class="blue_text"><i> permit membership in</i></font> the JROTC program for a homeschooled pupil who resides within the attendance area of the local educational agency and meets all applicable eligibility requirements for participation in the JROTC program other than enrollment in the school offering the JROTC program.</div><font color="#B30000"><strike><s><p style="margin-left: 1em;">(2)<span class="EnSpace"/>A local educational agency offering a JROTC program shall ensure equal access to the JROTC program for a pupil who resides within the attendance area of the local educational agency, is enrolled in a private school, independent study, or a public school other than the school offering the JROTC program, and meets all applicable eligibility requirements for participation in the program other than enrollment in the school offering the JROTC program.</s></p><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;"></div></strike></font><font color="blue" class="blue_text"><i><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;margin-left: 1em;">(2) For purposes of this subdivision, “homeschooled pupil” has the same meaning as the term “homeschooled student” used in Section 2031(f)(1) of Title 10 of the United States Code.</div></i></font><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">(d) The department shall make information about existing JROTC programs, including eligibility and application requirements for pupils described in subdivision (c), available on its internet website and distribute implementation guidance to local educational agencies on an annual basis.</div><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">(e) For purposes of this section,<font color="#B30000"><strike> the following definitions apply:</strike></font><font color="blue" class="blue_text"><i> “local educational agency” means a school district,
						charter school, or county office of education.</i></font></div><font color="#B30000"><strike><s><p style="margin-left: 1em;">(1)<span class="EnSpace"/>“Ensure equal access to the JROTC program” means to provide the same opportunities in relation to the JROTC program as provided to the pupils enrolled in the school offering the program.</s></p><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;"></div><s><p style="margin-left: 1em;">(2)<span class="EnSpace"/>“Local educational agency” means a school district, charter school, or county office of education.</s></p><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;"></div></strike></font></p></div></div></div></div></div></div></body></html>
